WEBVTT

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.980
Hello.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.720
Ryo-kun, come take care of your bags.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.320
Okay!

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:37.170
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:43.000
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.670
umetsukusu jouhou
Immersing information

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:50.670
ikigurushii kono joukyou
This suffocating situation

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:53.850
jibun ga inai
I'm not here

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.980
kono sekai no bousou
The world is going out of control

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:02.350
tada musekinin ni toubou
Run away irresponsibly

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.860
dokoe ikuno
Where am I going?

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.360
Huriyamanu ameni
The never-ending rain

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.130
zubunure oitekareta kokoro ga
Soak the neglected heart

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.040
kuzure yuku chokuzen no koe wo kike
Listen to the voices before it collapses

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:22.640
sasayakana kizunade ii
I'm fine with the subtle connection

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.750
sotto anata wo dakishimeru kara
I will hold you gently

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:40.400
kasaneta inochi ga
yukkurito ima kokyuu shite iru
The overlapped souls breathe slowly

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.100
sobani iruyo
"I'll be by your side."

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:49.940
Oh ware izukoe
Oh, where am I?

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:55.770
Oh ware yobukoe
Oh, the voice that's calling me

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.250
I've been looking for you.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.830
Smoking is prohibited on the premises.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.130
It's not lit.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.240
The status result from three days ago.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.780
No deaths, fortunately, but the
number of Apathy Syndrome victims...

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:43.390
It's not as bad as ten years ago, but cases
where this many people contract it at once...

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.790
They've surely asked about the cause.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:47.560
Yes.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.360
What did you tell them?

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.220
That it's still under investigation.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.230
We're the same.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.710
The Chief and us.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:04.710
Even if there weren't press
regulations, that's all I could say...

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.590
Have you gotten a hold of him?

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.040
No.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.760
Niichan?

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.500
Shin hasn't been in since this morning.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.640
He was back late last night, right?

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:42.980
Seemed like it.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.250
Does he say where he's going?

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.980
Nope.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.350
It probably means he wants to be alone.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.810
He's really good.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:38.640
Yeah.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.230
I wonder if he's gonna go to an art school?

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.010
I don't think he's considered it yet.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:48.080
I see. Well, he's got other things
besides his future to think about now.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:54.450
The brother came back after half a
year with a Persona from his dreams...

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.160
I mean, I guess he didn't "come back."

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.790
But you should be glad...

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.260
...he's still alive.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:14.030
You could've received a call
unexpectedly to hear he was dead.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.170
You still have to hope that as long as
he's alive, one day you'll see him again.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:20.740
Yeah.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:05:59.380
Morimoto?

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.640
I'm sorry. Um, I...

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.730
You dropped this, too.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.350
So, you had it.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.210
Yes.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.350
Is it working for you?

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.710
Good.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.520
I should give it back to you.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.460
Don't worry. If it's working, you should keep it.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:42.930
Thank you.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.560
Do you come here often?

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.040
Yamasaki told me about it a while ago.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:51.700
This place looks similar to the facility
grounds where you two used to live.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.800
Yes. I do, sometimes.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.770
Um, Kanzato-kun?

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.140
Huh?

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.910
Um, w-well...

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:04.310
What's your future goal?

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:11.280
Umm... Nothing special, at the moment.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.750
I'm sorry. This wasn't an appropriate time.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.630
Are you looking to go into
translation or something?

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:23.790
Oh, sorry. I saw a pamphlet for a
foreign language institute earlier.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.570
My teacher recommended it to me...

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.540
You are very smart.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:34.480
No... I'm good at memorizing,
but not applying the knowledge...

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:37.010
I'm bad at either one.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.150
Yeah...

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:43.120
Oh, I mean, no, I don't think so!

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:47.220
You're artistic, athletic...

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.230
and so kind.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:54.390
I-I should go home now. I'm sorry!

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.630
Hey, Morimoto...

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.180
Beef bowl ramen, huh?

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.930
Delivery!

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.860
Come in.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.100
You can leave it there.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.560
Counselor.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.130
I need to speak with you.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:41.210
I'd like to know the truth about
what you, former chief Kanzato,

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:45.740
and headquarters executives are covering up.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.060
What we witnessed three days ago...

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.190
Isn't everything related to that?

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:59.130
Apathy Syndrome, Reverse cases,
and ten years ago?

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.840
As you suspected,

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:06.470
I came here to silence
everything related to Personas.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.170
Officially, anyway.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:14.210
Please, have a seat.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.050
I'm home, Rune!

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:24.020
I'm home...

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.230
Of course he's not back.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.360
Hey, welcome back.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:11.540
I-I'm home.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.140
Sorry, but could you get the plates?

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:21.840
Who is this?

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.700
Go on. Eat up.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:39.730
I made it with what was available,
but it's pretty good.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.800
E-excuse me...

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:54.170
Do you have any isotonic water?

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:57.170
We have some bottled water.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:01.620
They're good for you when
you don't have an appetite.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:03.390
Buy some.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.160
Right...

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.330
When did it start coming out?

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:12.800
What?

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.500
Your Persona.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:20.670
How well are you able to use it?

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.700
Persona... you say?

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:24.910
That's right.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.820
It's... not like I can use it.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:32.240
It came out a few times when I was in danger.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.490
Hey, Shin!

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:34.150
Yes?

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:37.360
Is this water... old?

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:41.800
You're right.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:46.600
Young, growing men should not
undervalue water, the source of all life!

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:49.170
I-I'm sorry.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:54.230
Oh, the tap water in this area comes
from a natural spring, so it's pretty tasty.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:04.980
Um... May I ask who you are?

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:07.550
Sanada Akihiko.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.290
First of all, eat.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.180
Let's talk about your brother.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.190
Takuro, where's Kanzato-kun?

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:25.230
Oh...

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:27.340
What about your work? Are you off?

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:30.510
I'm going there in a bit. I got the late shift.

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:36.010
Don't you have to study?

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:37.680
I am.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:41.690
You're gonna go full-time at Sexy Dynamite?

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.380
It's Sexual Bomber!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.960
Same difference.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:49.050
Then, you should get certified as...

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.320
I know!

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:54.290
You need to be more considerate.

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:56.200
About what?

00:12:58.310 --> 00:12:58.960
Hey!

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.370
You two, do you have time?

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:14.180
Um...

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.610
What's up, Inui-san?

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:24.530
Marebito?

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:29.570
Multiple Personas were embedded in their psyche.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:33.530
Regardless of their compatibility,
they were made into Persona users.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:38.980
You were attacked by them several times, right?

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:42.250
The one who went out of control
three days ago was also one of them.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:51.990
They forcefully extract others' Personas and
absorb them into their own artificial one.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:58.890
Reverse is the term we use to refer to
the bodies of those attacked by them.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.340
But why?

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:05.000
We haven't gotten to the bottom of that.

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:12.800
However, it's clear they are conducting unnatural
research and unreasonably killing people.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:23.190
Ayanagi City is considered
brimming with Persona latents.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:26.130
How do you know that?

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:31.660
We gathered as much through research
Kanzato Ryo and I were involved in.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:36.900
Another theory says the
population increased ten years ago

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:40.930
after the Toyama Bay Apathy Syndrome outbreak.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:52.150
Even though the number's been declining,
Ayanagi City is still ideal for the Marebito.

00:14:55.760 --> 00:15:00.160
We were able to predict
someone like them beforehand.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:05.490
To fight back, we needed natural
latents with high abilities.

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:10.570
We needed to find Persona users among kids.

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.600
We used Shadow Extraction as one such method.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:17.010
What!?

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:23.180
We don't know who started it, or how, but
its effect correlates to the Persona's power.

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:32.080
We decided to find the kids with
high abilities based on those rumors.

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:33.420
Rumors!?

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:34.660
Rumors!?

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:36.060
That's right.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:41.430
How can officials do that sort
of thing based on rumors?

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:45.960
Rumors among kids are fairly reliable,
especially regarding issues like this.

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:50.000
We believe they're mostly accurate,
despite sounding meaningless.

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:54.420
That's why you knew so much
about Shadow Extraction,

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:57.910
and leave the dorms past curfew,
even though you're the manager.

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:01.650
But the Marebito had the same idea.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.580
Only, they seemed to have a more effective way...

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:10.920
Half a year ago, we completely fell behind them.

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:13.630
And what was the effective way?

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:19.810
If they didn't get ahead, Takashi,
Tasaka-senpai, and the other Reverse victims...

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.870
...wouldn't have had to go through that!

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:26.410
Why couldn't you have protected them earlier!?

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:29.820
Plus, even if it was to find strong Persona users,

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:34.150
many kids became apathetic
due to Shadow Extraction!

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:35.750
Look at Morimoto, too!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.620
All we can do is apologize.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.490
Then...

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:44.260
The list aniki had...

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.870
Can I listen, too?

00:16:57.340 --> 00:17:02.080
Kanzato and I were involved in
plans to establish a special force.

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:08.580
A Persona Force, formed only of those with high
enough abilities to handle supernatural cases.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:13.220
However...

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:16.760
The plan fell through within a year.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:20.560
There was strong opposition from various fields.

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:28.640
Then, something came up we
couldn't do anything about.

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:31.580
The age limit.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:40.880
There's no specific age set, but we know when
a person is old enough to become an officer,

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.590
their Persona can no longer be used.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:45.520
But Ryo-niichan was...

00:17:47.260 --> 00:17:51.290
You could keep using it by taking
a certain drug, as a sole exception.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:59.810
It's the same substance
regulating Complex Personas.

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:02.540
Why would he go so far?

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.540
A sense of duty.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.280
He didn't say much to me, either.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:12.620
He voiced his desire to resume the plan,

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:17.320
and even after cancellation, kept in
touch with the development leader.

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:20.360
That's how aware he was of this crisis.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:26.500
After a while, a special force to prevent Persona
misuse was established at headquarters.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.970
Candidly speaking, our only
task was to smudge the truth.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:37.610
Even above us, there are people
who belong to the other side.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:42.980
Fighting against the Marebito is
a lonely task with no support.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.920
Even so... Whoever is capable must commit to it.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:56.300
Sanada-san...

00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:59.690
Was that... our brother?

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:02.830
I don't know.

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:11.870
Ito Kunio
Kanzato

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:16.380
The message was passed to the appropriate people.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:18.950
Now it's all up to them.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.450
Here, too.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:52.250
Did you already know about his Persona?

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:54.010
Yeah.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:55.180
I see.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.080
We'll just have to ask him in person, right?

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:05.120
Yeah.

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:17.900
Kanzato Shigeru Kanzato Haruka
Kanzato Yuki

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.010
Were you?

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:33.220
It's a coincidence.

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:40.400
Ito Yuuna

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:49.440
It's me.

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.870
Roger that. Don't you take
your eyes off of him, Narasaki!

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:59.940
And... make sure to report to Sanada.

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:02.820
Ito-san.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:09.990
Thank you for taking me back to the
dorms the other day without a question.

00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:13.630
I ended up calling you a buncha times, though.

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.970
But it's all fine now. I got most of it.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:17.700
I...

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:19.870
No need.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:23.970
Just think about your brother's feelings.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:58.010
Itsukara yume miru koto
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:21:58.010 --> 00:22:03.420
Wasureta huri wo shitetan darou
When did I start pretending
like I didn't dream of anything?

00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:10.720
Chiisana mado akeru yuuki mo naku
With no courage to open a small
window, I waited for a miracle.

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:16.060
Kiseki wo matteta
With no courage to open a small
window, I waited for a miracle.

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:25.710
Ushinau mono nado nakatta anohi no yona
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:31.110
mujakisa wa mou naikedo
I'm not as innocent as I used to be in
the days when I had nothing to lose

00:22:31.110 --> 00:22:37.680
namida wo nugutta ato niwa
After wiping away the tears

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:43.720
atarashii jibun ni deaeru
I'll be able to meet a new self

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:47.530
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
Even if I lose everything

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:53.730
subete wo nakushitemo
mitsuke rareru monoga arukara
There are still some things to discover

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:59.570
kesenai kizumo itsuka
Even the scars that remain

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:05.940
watashi rashii hokori ni dekiru
will someday become my pride

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:14.960
Time for those without masters.

00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:20.220
Even extended, it eventually comes to an end.

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:25.330
Even before arriving, or after departing,

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:27.320
they are destined to wander.

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:31.700
The hurt, honored guest with no home.

00:23:32.240 --> 00:23:35.040
The parting and gathering of consciousness.

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:38.910
The harmony and silence that must exist.
